title: "CGPA to Percentage Calculator (and Percentage to CGPA)"
description: "Convert CGPA to percentage or percentage to CGPA on a 4.0, 5.0 or 10.0 scale using simple proportion, the CBSE 9.5 rule, or your transcript formula."
permalink: /tools/cgpa-to-percentage-calculator/
h1: "CGPA to Percentage Calculator"
extraCss: "/tools/cgpa-to-percentage-calculator/style.css"
quickAnswer: "With the simple proportion method, percentage = CGPA ÷ scale × 100, so a 3.2 CGPA on a 4.0 scale is 80% and 3.5 is 87.5%. CBSE's 10-point rule is CGPA × 9.5, so 8.0 becomes 76%. If your transcript prints its own conversion, that formula is the official one for your degree."
formula:
  title: "CGPA to Percentage Formulas"
  expression: "Percentage = CGPA ÷ Scale × 100"
  explanation: "This simple proportion treats your CGPA as a share of the maximum CGPA. For CBSE's 10-point scale the conversion is Percentage = CGPA × 9.5. If your university prints its own formula in the form Percentage = m × CGPA + c, use that instead. Going the other way, each formula is solved for CGPA: CGPA = Percentage ÷ 100 × Scale, CGPA = Percentage ÷ 9.5, or CGPA = (Percentage − c) ÷ m."
  variables:
    - name: "Scale"
      description: "The maximum CGPA on your system: 4.0, 5.0 or 10.0."
    - name: "m and c"
      description: "The multiplier and offset in your university's printed conversion, if it has one."
workedExamples:
  - title: "3.2 CGPA on a 4.0 scale (simple proportion)"
    inputs:
      - "CGPA: 3.2"
      - "Scale: 4.0"
